<title>CHILE: Chile Enami regional workers accept pay offer.</title>
<headline>Chile Enami regional workers accept pay offer.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at the regional offices of Enami have accepted a five year collective labor contract, the state mining and smelting company said.</p>
<p>The vote last week means that 70 percent of Enami's workforce have accepted the new pay deal, said the statement.</p>
<p>Union members at Enami's Ventanas smelting and refining complex are now the only ones still in talks to renew the plant's collective contract which expires on January 31.</p>
<p>Negotiations began this month at Ventanas which smelts 126,000 tonnes of copper a year and has a refining capacity of 330,000 tonnes.</p>
</text>
